\"Rare material - see Text\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Multichain at F3 to get all but the enemy at B5. All Strange enemies, what fun. The KP Chance is a 10-second win, not a problem. As we fight, the moogle tells us more and more, revealing all his secrets at last. By this time, if it wasn't long ago, it should be perfectly clear who he really is. If you've read the reports, you know.\n</p><p>First, a Level 100 Counterfeit Youth, he has a couple hundred HP with an Iifa Leaf, summons Mandragora, and spams Firaga. Then comes a Level 100 Fleeting Flash who uses Bahamut and Crushing Blow. Then, a Level 100 Ephemeral Vision with Wither Shot, Energy Rain and Jecht Shot. Now a Level 100 Phantasmal Harlequin with Deathgaze and Forsaken. Then, a Level 100 Idle Sky Pirate with Gilgamesh and Windburst. Last are a Level 100 Imaginary Champion with Bahamut and Octaslash and a Level 100 Delusory Knight with Carbuncle and most of Cecil's HP attacks.\n</p><p>The one chest has a Diamond Ring. The other has a random trade accessory from the following: Dragon's Seal, Chocograph, Omega Badge, Wyvern Egg, Whisperweed, Occult Fan, Al Bhed Primer, Shinra Card Key, Snowboard, Sphere, Gnomish Bread, Strategy Guide, Carnelian Signet, Automaton Parts, Warp Cube, Noah's Lute, Crystal Eye, GF Eden, Wild Rose, Delicious Fish, Nethicite, Tintinabulum. These items cannot be bought or traded for, and are needed for a lot of equipment, two each for each equipment piece associated with a \"Recipe\" trade item. The most important are the Ultima Weapon (Pisces Recipe, Noah's Lute, Whisperweed, Level 100 and usable by anyone and gives +2 ATK and DEF at full HP), Dangerously Lucky (Gemini Recipe, Gnomish Bread, Automaton Parts, Last Chance like an Iifa Leaf and +75% item drop), Bone Mail (Scorpio Recipe, Wild Rose, Occult Fan, no EX absorption, useful for some builds), and the Ensanguined Shield (Taurus Recipe, Wyvern Egg, Snowboard, HP -95% on battle start and Bravery 0, also useful for some builds).\n</p><p>On to the next gateway.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">I\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">J\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Rare Material - see Text\"><img alt=\"Rare Material - see Text\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a hr